### Demo 0, Lab 10: HTTP essentials against a public API (no backend of ours yet).
### Run these in IntelliJ or the VS Code REST Client, and the same ones with curl from the guide.

### 1. GET: a resource. Look at the status line, Content-Type and the JSON shape.
GET https://dummyjson.com/products/1
Accept: application/json

### 2. A resource that does not exist: the status code is the answer, not the body.
GET https://dummyjson.com/products/99999

### 3. A collection with query parameters: paging lives in the URL.
GET https://dummyjson.com/products?limit=3&skip=3&select=title,price

### 4. POST: send JSON, get 201 and the created resource back. Content-Type tells the server what you sent.
POST https://dummyjson.com/products/add
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "ShopScope stoneware mug", "price": 499}

### 5. PUT vs PATCH: replace vs change some fields.
PATCH https://dummyjson.com/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"price": 549}

### 6. DELETE: idempotent. Send it twice; the second answer is the point.
DELETE https://dummyjson.com/products/1
